                <pb facs="1410" n="1396" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1396"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/7–844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stewart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-08">July 8, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>296. The Nicaraguan Embassy here, under direct instructions from President
                    Somoza, has expressed the President’s indignation that an opposition political
                    group on July 4 should have used the American flag in a parade and meeting.</p>
                <p>Please report by telegram regarding this incident.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
